# 🩺 CKD Prediction Web App | Machine Learning + Flask

## 📌 Project Overview

The **CKD Prediction Web App** is a Machine Learning-based web application developed to predict the possibility of **Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)** using clinical patient parameters.

The project combines **Machine Learning, Python, Flask, SQL database management, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript** into an interactive web application.

Users can enter patient clinical information through the web interface, and the trained Machine Learning model generates a prediction. The application also provides patient record management and PDF report generation.

---

## 🎯 Project Objective

The main objective of this project is to develop a web-based system that can use clinical parameters to generate a CKD prediction.

### Objectives

- Build a Machine Learning model for CKD prediction.
- Preprocess and prepare clinical data for model training.
- Integrate the trained model with a Flask application.
- Create an interactive patient data entry interface.
- Store patient information and prediction results.
- Generate downloadable patient PDF reports.
- Demonstrate the practical implementation of Machine Learning in a web application.

---

## 🧩 Problem Statement

Chronic Kidney Disease can develop gradually and may not always produce noticeable symptoms during its early stages.

This project explores how Machine Learning can be used with selected clinical parameters to identify patterns associated with CKD and provide a prediction through a web-based application.

The application is designed as an **educational and demonstration project** and is not intended to replace professional medical diagnosis.

---

## 📊 Dataset

The project uses a preprocessed clinical dataset:

**Dataset:** `CKD_Preprocessed.csv`

The dataset contains clinical parameters used for Machine Learning development.

### Clinical Parameters

| Parameter | Description |
|---|---|
| Age | Patient age |
| Blood Pressure | Patient blood pressure |
| Specific Gravity | Urine specific gravity |
| Albumin | Albumin level |
| Sugar | Sugar level |
| Blood Glucose | Random blood glucose level |
| Blood Urea | Blood urea level |
| Serum Creatinine | Serum creatinine level |
| Hemoglobin | Hemoglobin level |
| Hypertension | Hypertension status |
| Diabetes Mellitus | Diabetes status |
| Anemia | Anemia status |

